{"archetypes":[{"name":"state-machine","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"Diff relocates /design sentinels and FINALIZE across fresh and paused paths.","prompt_body":"Investigate the /design step state machine around Step 2a, Step 2a.5, Step 3b, Step 4, and Gate C. Check whether sentinel creation, compatibility guards, and resume routing remain idempotent and cannot skip required artifacts on SIMPLE, HARD, degraded, and old paused sessions. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"bash-fences","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"Embedded Bash fences now own fail-fast writes and FINALIZE failure propagation.","prompt_body":"Review the changed embedded Bash fences in SKILL.md and the shell harness additions. Focus on set -e/set +e interactions, captured exit statuses, quoting, bash 3.2 portability, and whether completion markers are written only after successful artifact operations. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"routing-sync","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"Routing prose and script breadcrumbs must stay synchronized across multiple canonical docs.","prompt_body":"Trace every updated Step 3b-to-Step 4 route across the skill prompt, approval gates, flags reference, configuration docs, and run-step3-review output. Look for stale direct routes, ambiguous shorthand, or wording that lets an operator bypass the Step 3b completion boundary. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"harness-regex","focus_area":"code-quality","weight":1,"rationale":"The structure harness adds line-scoped and fence-scoped parsing that could be brittle or under/over-match.","prompt_body":"Examine the new test-design-structure.sh parsing and assertions for brittleness. Check whether awk, grep, marker slicing, and line-scoped route detection accurately cover the intended regions without false positives or blind spots. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
